At Mon, 13 Nov 2006 16:04:10 +0300,
Andrew L. Neporada wrote:
> 
> Hi!
> 
> It seems that snd_hda_intel driver fails to detect hp/mic/line jack
> presense with ALC883 codec.
> 
> According to Realtek's specs (and practice) ALC883 doesn't generate
> unsolicited events in this case,

Really?  AFAIK, all port pins can generate unsolicited events,
according to the datasheet version 1.2 (see section 8.21).

> so the only way to detect jack is to
> periodically poll appropriate pin complex with AC_VERB_GET_PIN_SENSE.
> AFAIK, there is currently no way to do such thing.
> 
> The idea is to add a new function to hda_codec_ops:
>   void (*poll)(struct hda_codec *codec)
> and run it as a separate thread after codec init phase is done.

I don't think we need a common callback for this particular codec.
Each codec routine can create a workqueue if needed.


Takashi

